Search "lighting ideas for wedding rentals" and most guides list uplighting, gobo projection, chandeliers, candles and color washes, a full decor catalog. Malaga Event Gear (MEG) doesn't stock most of that. Our wedding lighting packages bundle two things: fairy lights and warm LED strings on the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/), and RGBW color changing spotlights on the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/). We also stock a wireless uplighting kit as a separate item, not bundled into either package. This guide covers exactly where each package option works and how to choose between them, not a wishlist of fixtures we don't rent. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview.

## Brief Overview

---

MEG's wedding lighting packages come down to two real products, not forty seven ideas. The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) includes fairy lights and warm LED strings for up to 80 guests, a static, warm glow with a live technician on site, for 650 euros ex VAT. The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) includes 2 light bars with RGBW LED spotlights for up to 50 guests, a color changing accent option you run yourself, for 290 euros ex VAT. Neither package includes uplighting, chandeliers, candles, lanterns or gobo projection: uplighting is real, but a separate quote on request item, not part of either package.

## Key Highlights

---

-   MEG's wedding lighting is two real products: fairy lights and warm LED strings on the Wedding Pack, RGBW color changing spotlights on the Eco Pack. Nothing else.
-   The Wedding Pack's fairy lights create a warm, static glow, not color changing light. That effect belongs to the Eco Pack's RGBW spotlights instead.
-   Placement matters more than fixture count: pergolas, beams, trees and walkways all take fairy lights differently at Malaga area venues.
-   Guest count and whether you want static warmth or color changing accents decide which package fits, not a strict upgrade path from one to the other.
-   We stock a wireless uplighting kit as a separate, quote on request item, not bundled into either wedding package. We don't offer gobo or monogram projection, chandeliers, candles, lanterns or LED path lighting. See [essential items for wedding rentals](/blog/essential-items-for-wedding-rentals/) for the full list of what MEG does and doesn't rent.

## What MEG's Wedding Lighting Actually Is, and Isn't

Search results for this keyword are dominated by decor blogs listing fifteen to twenty lighting styles: uplighting, pin spot lighting, gobo and monogram projection, chandeliers, drapery lighting, disco and dance floor color washes, candles, lanterns, solar and battery lights, LED path lighting. MEG's wedding packages bundle two fixtures: fairy lights and warm LED strings on the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/), and RGBW LED spotlights on the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/). Uplighting is real too, but a separate item quoted on request, not part of either package. Everything else on that list, gobo and monogram projection, chandeliers, drapery, candles and lanterns, we don't stock. A venue's own lighting, or a decorator's chandeliers and candles, come from the venue or a separate stylist, not from us. Our [indoor wedding rental essentials](/blog/indoor-wedding-rental-essentials/) guide covers how our lighting sits as an accent layer on top of a venue's existing fixtures, and our [unique wedding ceremony rentals](/blog/unique-wedding-ceremony-rentals/) guide covers the same point for a ceremony space specifically.

<InlineCTA />

## Where Fairy Lights Actually Work at Malaga Venues

The Wedding Pack's fairy lights and warm LED strings are a single, warm, static glow: no color changes, no dimming scenes, no chasing patterns. What varies is where they go, and that's where the real planning happens. At the pergolas common to fincas and villas around Malaga, strings run along the beams and cross bracing, turning a bare wooden structure into a lit canopy once the sun goes down. Strung between trees, or along a walkway from parking to the ceremony or reception area, they mark the route guests actually walk, doing double duty as light and wayfinding. Draped directly over a reception area, whether that's a marquee frame, a row of beams, or simply run point to point across an open dining space, they replace the flat dark of an evening sky with a canopy of warm points overhead. In each case the fixture and the effect stay the same. What changes is where our technician physically anchors the strings on the day, based on what your specific venue offers to attach to.

## Choosing Between the Wedding Pack and the Eco Pack for Lighting

Two guests asking the same question, what lighting should I book, get different honest answers depending on guest count and the look they want. The [Wedding Pack's](/packages/wedding/) fairy lights suit a warm, romantic, unchanging glow for up to 80 guests, with a live technician on site to place and monitor the system throughout. The [Eco Pack's](/packages/eco/) RGBW spotlights suit a smaller event, up to 50 guests, where a color accent, lighting up a dance floor or washing the space in your palette, matters more than warmth, delivered, installed and tested by our crew, then run without a technician for the rest of the event. That same choice is part of the broader booking pattern we track in our [latest trends in wedding rentals](/blog/latest-trends-in-wedding-rentals/) guide.

| | Eco Pack | Wedding Pack |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Guest count | Up to 50 | Up to 80 |
| Technician on site | No, self run after setup | Yes, throughout the event |
| Lighting | RGBW LED spotlights, color changing | Fairy lights and warm LED strings, static warm glow |
| Price | 290 euros ex VAT | 650 euros ex VAT |

This isn't an upgrade path from one to the other. They're two different lighting looks for two different event sizes. A couple planning a larger reception who also wants color changing accents needs to discuss that combination with us directly rather than assume the Wedding Pack includes it, since as delivered, it doesn't.

