## FAQs

### How much does wedding lighting rental cost?

MEG's wedding lighting comes bundled inside two packages rather than sold separately. The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) includes fairy lights and warm LED strings for 650 euros ex VAT, and the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) includes RGBW spotlights for 290 euros ex VAT. Both prices cover the full package, sound and microphones included, not lighting alone.

### What's the difference between uplighting and spotlighting?

Uplighting sits on the floor and washes light upward against a wall or structure. Spotlighting aims a narrow beam at a specific point, like a table or the couple. We stock both: a wireless uplighting kit of 6 fixtures as a separate quote on request item, and the [Eco Pack's](/packages/eco/) RGBW light bars for a fixed position spotlight and color accent. Neither is bundled into the Wedding Pack, so [contact us](/contact/) if your reception needs uplighting alongside it. For the full spec on that kit, honest coverage for 2 to 4 venue features, and a direct comparison against these RGBW spotlights, see our [stage uplighting](/blog/stage-uplighting/) guide.

### Can wedding lighting include gobo or monogram projection?

Not through MEG. Gobo and monogram projection, casting a couple's initials or a pattern onto a wall or floor, isn't part of either package. If that's specifically what you're after, it needs a separate specialty lighting vendor. Our [essential items for wedding rentals](/blog/essential-items-for-wedding-rentals/) guide covers the full line of what MEG does and doesn't rent.

### Where should fairy lights be placed at an outdoor wedding?

Pergola beams, trees along a walkway, and directly over a reception area are the three placements that come up most at Malaga area venues. Wind and what the structure can actually hold decide the exact anchoring on the day, which our [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guide covers in more depth for the rest of the outdoor setup.

### Does any MEG lighting change color for the dance floor?

Yes, but only on the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/), whose RGBW light bars produce color changing light suited to a dance floor. The [Wedding Pack's](/packages/wedding/) fairy lights and warm LED strings stay a fixed warm tone and don't change color, an important distinction if a color changing dance floor look is specifically what you want.
